-- title:
--   Residual χ∘det block of the σ-twisted spectral side
-- statement:
--   Fix number fields $K \subseteq L$ with $L/K$ finite and Galois, and reals $0 < \alpha < \beta$.
--
--   **Global fundamental-domain data.** A set $\Phi_L \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ is given which lies in the slab $\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$ (here $\|\cdot\|$ is [`NumberField.TateGlobal.ideleNorm`](def/NumberField_TateGlobalZeta.html#L19), the module of the idele acting on $\mathbb{A}_L$) and which, by `hΦ`, is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under `globalPoints` acting on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, with respect to the Haar measure `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L` restricted to that slab.
--
--   **Centre data.** A Haar measure $\nu_{Z}$ on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ is given together with a set $\Omega_L \subseteq \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ which is a fundamental domain for the image of $L^\times$ in $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ with respect to $\nu_Z$.
--
--   **Galois data.** $D$ is an `IdeleGaloisDescent` datum for $(\mathcal{O}_L, K, L)$, i.e. a homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K) \to \mathrm{RingAut}(\mathbb{A}_L)$ whose value at each $\tau$ is continuous and compatible with $\tau$ on principal adeles; $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$, and `hgen` requires every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to lie in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$).
--
--   **Ramification and central-character data.** $S_L$ is a finite set of finite places of $L$ which by `hSL` is a union of fibres over $K$ (for all $w,w'$ lying under the same place of $K$, $w \in S_L \iff w' \in S_L$); $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top \le \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ with `hξc` its continuity as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function and `hξt` its triviality on principal ideles; $N$ is an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_L$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S_L$ (`hN`); and $\mathrm{tys}_L$ is an `ArchTypeFamily` for $L$, i.e. a finite list of archimedean types `rep w i` at each infinite place $w$.
--
--   **Test-function skeleton.** $S$ is a finite set of finite places of $K$, $\varphi_a$ a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$, and $\varphi_S$ assigns to each finite place $v$ of $K$ a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$.
--
--   **Table space.** $X$ is a set of tables $x : \{\text{finite places of } L\} \to \mathbb{C} \times \mathbb{C}$, and `hX` requires $X$ to contain every table $x$ with $x_w = 0$ for all $w \in S_L$ and, for all $w \notin S_L$, $(x_w)_2 = \mathrm{cNorm}(w)\,\xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}(w))$, $\|(x_w)_1\| \le (\mathrm{Nm}(w)+1)\sqrt{\|\xi_L(\det \mathrm{heckeGen}(w))\|}$, and $\overline{(x_w)_1} = \big(\overline{(x_w)_2}/\|(x_w)_2\|\big)(x_w)_1$, where $\mathrm{cNorm}(w) = \mathrm{Nm}(w) =$ `Ideal.absNorm w.asIdeal`.
--
--   **Siegel covering data.** Reals $c,u,d_1,d_2$ with $0 < c$, a compact set $T_c \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, and a second set $\Phi_0$ which (i) is contained in the union over $y \in T_c$ of the right translates by $y$ of the centre-cut Siegel set `WindowedSiegel.centreCutSiegelSet L c u d₁ d₂` (finite part integral, all local heights $\ge c$, all window quantities $\le u^2$, all archimedean determinant norms in $[d_1,d_2]$), (ii) lies in the slab $\{\|\det g\| \in [\alpha,\beta]\}$, and (iii) is again a fundamental domain for $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ for the slab-restricted Haar measure.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a sequence of tables $\mathrm{tabs} : \mathbb{N} \to (\{\text{finite places of }L\} \to \mathbb{C}\times\mathbb{C})$, a proof $\mathrm{htabs}$ that $\mathrm{tabs}\,n \in X$ for all $n$ (so that $\langle \mathrm{tabs}\,n, \mathrm{htabs}\,n\rangle$ is a point of $X$), and coefficients $\mathrm{cs} : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{C}$ such that the following three assertions hold.
--
--   *(1)* $\sum_n \|\mathrm{cs}\,n\| < \infty$.
--
--   *(2)* For every $n$ with $\mathrm{cs}\,n \ne 0$: first, $\mathrm{tabs}\,n$ is constant on fibres over $K$ outside $S_L$, i.e. $\mathrm{tabs}\,n\,w = \mathrm{tabs}\,n\,w'$ whenever $w, w' \notin S_L$ lie under the same place of $K$; second, there are a non-zero ideal $M$ of $\mathcal{O}_L$ and two homomorphisms $\chi_1,\chi_2 : \mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$, each continuous as a $\mathbb{C}$-valued function and trivial on principal ideles, such that for all $w \notin S_L$ the value $\mathrm{tabs}\,n\,w$ is the pair of Hecke parameters of the Eisenstein eigensystem [`LanglandsTunnell.Converse.eisensteinTableOf L M hM χ₁ χ₂`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ConverseData.html#L132) at $w$, namely $\big(\chi_1(\varpi_w)+\chi_2(\varpi_w),\ \chi_1(\varpi_w)\chi_2(\varpi_w)\big)$, where $\varpi_w =$ `uniformizerIdele` at $w$.
--
--   *(3)* For every finite set $T$ of finite places of $K$ with $T$ disjoint from $S$, $\#T \ge 2$, and such that no place of $L$ above a place of $T$ lies in $S_L$; for every choice of an extension place $\mathrm{ws}\,v$ of $L$ over each $v$, and of places $w'(v)$ of $L$ with $(w'(v))$ having ideal $\sigma^{-1} \cdot (\mathrm{ws}\,v)$ for $v \in T$; for every family $\varpi_v$ in the valuation ring of the completion $L_{\mathrm{ws}\,v}$ which is irreducible for $v \in T$, with nonzero image in $L_{\mathrm{ws}\,v}$ for $v \in T$ (hypothesis `hϖs0`); for all $n_v \in \mathbb{N}$ and families $r_{T,v} : \mathrm{Fin}(n_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{\mathrm{ws}\,v})$ such that for $v \in T$ the family $r_{T,v}$ is a Hecke coset system ([`HeckeIntegralSeam.IsHeckeCosetSystem`](def/LocalLanglands_HeckeCosetSystem.html#L15)) for the subgroup [`LocalGL2.integralSubgroup`](def/LocalLanglands_LocalHeckeInstance.html#L13) (the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the valuation ring) and the element $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi_v,1)$, i.e. its members lie in the double coset, they cover it modulo left-multiples of the subgroup, and they are pairwise distinct in the quotient; for every family $z_v \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{\mathrm{ws}\,v})$ with $z_v = \varpi_v \cdot 1$ for $v \in T$; for all $k_v, j_v \in \mathbb{N}$; for every continuous, compactly supported $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ and every $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles such that `IsSemiLocalFactorization K L (S ∪ T) φ φa φf` holds for the local data which at $v \in T$ is the function
--   $$x \mapsto \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(k_v) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_v)} \mathbf{1}_{\,\mathcal{I}_v}\Big(\big(\text{semi-local component at } v \text{ of the local embedding at } \mathrm{ws}\,v \text{ of } \textstyle\prod_m r_{T,v}(\iota\,m) \cdot z_v^{\,j_v}\big)^{-1} x\Big),$$
--   with $\mathcal{I}_v =$ `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v`, and at $v \notin T$ is $\varphi_S\,v$ — that factorisation hypothesis asserting that $\varphi_a$ is an archimedean test factor, $\varphi_f$ locally constant with compact support, each local factor at a place of $S \cup T$ locally constant with compact support, $\varphi_f(h) = \prod_{v \in S \cup T}$ (local factor at $v$) applied to the semi-local component of $h$ whenever all components outside $S \cup T$ are integral, $\varphi_f(h) = 0$ if some component outside $S\cup T$ is not integral, and $\varphi(g) = \varphi_a(g_\infty)\varphi_f(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$; and such moreover that $\varphi$ is bi-invariant under the subgroup `levelOne (𝓞 L) L N ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L` (level $N$ intersected with the kernel of the archimedean projection) and satisfies `IsArchBiFinite L tysL φ`, i.e. $g \mapsto \varphi(g^{-1})$ lies in the archimedean cut submodule and $\varphi$ in the archimedean dual cut submodule attached to $\mathrm{tys}_L$ —
--
--   then, for every continuous $g : X \to \mathbb{C}$ which is given on $X$ by the monomial
--   $$g(x) = \prod_{v \in T} \big(x_{w'(v)}\big)_1^{\,k_v} \cdot \Big(\mathrm{cNorm}(w'(v))^{-1}\big(x_{w'(v)}\big)_2\Big)^{\,j_v},$$
--   the following three statements hold, where for $x,y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ one puts
--   $$K^{\mathrm{res}}_\varphi(x,y) = \frac{\nu_{Z}\big(\Omega_L \cap \{z : \|\det(z\cdot 1)\|_{\mathbb{A}_L} \in [\alpha,\beta]\}\big)}{\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}(\Phi_0)} \cdot {\sum_{\chi \in \mathcal{X}}}^{\mathrm{f}} \big(\mathrm{twistedConvOp}\,K\,L\,D\,\sigma\,\varphi\,(\chi\circ\det)\big)(x)\,\cdot\,\chi^{-1}(\det y),$$
--   the two measures of sets being taken as real numbers and then as complex numbers, the sum being a `finsum` over the set $\mathcal{X}$ of homomorphisms $\chi : \mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$ with $\chi(z)^2 = \xi_L(z)$ for all ideles $z$, $\chi$ trivial on principal ideles and $\chi$ continuous, and $\mathrm{twistedConvOp}\,K\,L\,D\,\sigma\,\varphi\,u$ being the right convolution of $u \circ (\text{the automorphism } \mathrm{sigmaAdelicAct}\,K\,L\,D\,\sigma)$ against $\varphi$, that is $x \mapsto \int_{\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)} u\big(\mathrm{sigmaAdelicAct}(x y)\big)\varphi(y)\,d\mu(y)$. For $R \in \mathbb{R}$ let $\Lambda_R(x)$ denote the value at $x$ of the truncation [`AutomorphicForm.lambdaT`](def/AutomorphicForm_TruncationOperator.html#L48) at level $e^R$, applied in the second variable to $y \mapsto K^{\mathrm{res}}_\varphi(x,y)$: the truncation uses the unipotent family $t \mapsto \begin{pmatrix}1&t\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, the height function [`NumberField.AdelicHeight.adelicHeight L`](def/NumberField_AdelicHeight.html#L158), and the measurable space and measure fields of `productionPinsOf L ΦL (fun M => levelOne (𝓞 L) L M ⊓ finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup L) (heckeGen (𝓞 L) L) (adelicBox L)`, whose measure is the additive adelic Haar measure conditioned on the box `adelicBox L`; explicitly, $\Lambda_R(x) = K^{\mathrm{res}}_\varphi(x,x) - \mathbf{1}_{\{\mathrm{adelicHeight} > e^R\}}(x)\cdot(\text{constant term of } K^{\mathrm{res}}_\varphi(x,\cdot))(x)$.
--
--   The three statements are: (i) for every $R \in \mathbb{R}$ the function $x \mapsto \Lambda_R(x)$ is integrable on $\Phi_0$ with respect to `adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 L) L`; (ii) the series $\sum_n \mathrm{cs}\,n \cdot g\big(\langle \mathrm{tabs}\,n, \mathrm{htabs}\,n\rangle\big)$ is summable; and (iii) as $R \to \infty$,
--   $$\int_{\Phi_0} \Lambda_R(x)\,d\,\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}(x) \longrightarrow \sum_{n}' \mathrm{cs}\,n \cdot g\big(\langle \mathrm{tabs}\,n, \mathrm{htabs}\,n\rangle\big).$$
--
--   The tables $\mathrm{tabs}$ and coefficients $\mathrm{cs}$ are produced once and for all, before the quantification over $T$, the local Hecke data, $\varphi$ and $g$.
--
--   This is the residual block of the spectral side of the $\sigma$-twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension $L/K$: the kernel built from the one-dimensional automorphic constituents $\chi \circ \det$ with $\chi^2 = \xi_L$, truncated along the unipotent direction, is evaluated on the diagonal over a Siegel-covered fundamental domain and identified in the limit with an absolutely convergent sum of Hecke monomials over atoms whose eigensystems are Eisenstein tables. It feeds the assembly of the two sides of the twisted trace formula along Hecke words in [`AutomorphicForm.exists_atomic_forall_tendsto_setIntegral_lambdaT_finsum_integral_sigmaAdelicAct_centralScalar_sub_tsum_finsum_setIntegral_twistedConvOp_sub`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_atomic_forall_tendsto_setIntegral_lambdaT_finsum_integral_sigmaAdelicAct_centralScalar_sub_tsum_finsum_setIntegral_twistedConvOp_sub).
